# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets _headers file.
# Lives at the ASSETS ROOT (copied to dist-cf/_headers by build:cf — NOT under
# public/, which would nest it under /apps/filemark/ where CF ignores it).
# Path patterns match the request URL the worker sees, i.e. /apps/filemark/*.
#
# Scope note: deliberately NO Strict-Transport-Security or Content-Security-
# Policy here — HSTS is domain-wide and belongs to the parent khanakia.com
# gateway, and a wrong CSP would break GTM / inline scripts. These four are
# safe, universally-recommended hardening headers.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

# Hashed build assets are content-addressed — cache them forever.
/apps/filemark/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
